vLLM-MetaX: reduce Flash Attention metadata overhead

Base: vLLM-MetaX v0.17.0 (14d1f8889bf08c3a368f572d885d04f95ea88dfb)
Result-Tree: fdc9fc6d847e624dad59fd0e6106f5619e16abdc
Target: vllm_metax/v1/attention/backends/flash_attn.py

Feature 1:
Use the existing batch max_seq_len as a safe prefill upper bound instead of
prefill_seq_lens.max().item(). This removes a device-to-host scalar sync and
the associated mcStreamSynchronize wait from metadata construction.

Feature 2:
Do not precompute cu_seqlens_k in the Non-DCP metadata path. The forward path
rebuilds the value from seq_lens before invoking Flash Attention, so the old
zero_/to/pad/cumsum work was redundant GPU kernel and launch overhead.

Scope:
The DCP path is unchanged. The patch changes metadata preparation only and
does not modify MetaX kernels, Flash Attention kernel inputs, or mcoplib APIs.
Inline comments are included beside both optimizations.

---
diff --git a/vllm_metax/v1/attention/backends/flash_attn.py b/vllm_metax/v1/attention/backends/flash_attn.py
index 94e5807b0e98c2f0ee74b57d76b143d0687c68b0..5ad895911c73f6ff60eaf578916ddf3309f0496c 100644
--- a/vllm_metax/v1/attention/backends/flash_attn.py
+++ b/vllm_metax/v1/attention/backends/flash_attn.py
@@ -489,7 +489,9 @@ class FlashAttentionMetadataBuilder(AttentionMetadataBuilder[FlashAttentionMetad
                 - common_attn_metadata.query_start_loc[num_decodes]
             )
             prefill_seq_lens = common_attn_metadata.seq_lens[num_decodes:num_reqs]
-            prefill_max_seq_len = int(prefill_seq_lens.max().item())
+            # Use the existing batch max as a safe upper bound to avoid a
+            # device-to-host sync from prefill_seq_lens.max().item().
+            prefill_max_seq_len = max_seq_len
             prefill_block_table_tensor = common_attn_metadata.block_table_tensor[
                 num_decodes:num_reqs
             ]
@@ -618,25 +620,9 @@ class FlashAttentionMetadataBuilder(AttentionMetadataBuilder[FlashAttentionMetad
                 causal=causal,
             )
 
-            # --------------------------------------------------------------
-            # Note: Precompute cu_seqlens_k (prefix sums over KV lengths) on GPU.
-            # This replaces any forward-time construction that would require
-            # CPU sync (e.g. via .tolist()), which breaks CUDA graph capture.
-            if self.use_full_cuda_graph:
-                if self._cu_seqlens_k_buffer is not None:
-                    n = num_reqs + 1
-                    buf = self._cu_seqlens_k_buffer
-                    # Leading 0, then inclusive cumsum into buf[1:n].
-                    buf[0].zero_()
-                    seq_lens_i32 = seq_lens[:num_reqs].to(dtype=torch.int32)
-                    torch.cumsum(seq_lens_i32, dim=0, dtype=torch.int32, out=buf[1:n])
-                    cu_seqlens_k = buf[:n]
-                else:
-                    cu_seqlens_k = F.pad(
-                        seq_lens[:num_reqs],
-                        (1, 0),
-                        value=0,
-                    ).cumsum(dim=0, dtype=torch.int32)
+            # Non-DCP forward rebuilds cu_seqlens_k from seq_lens immediately
+            # before the Flash Attention call, so leave the metadata value as
+            # None here and avoid redundant zero_/to/pad/cumsum GPU kernels.
 
         # For FA3 + full cudagraph
         if self.use_full_cuda_graph and scheduler_metadata is not None:
